{"tool_name":"pathwaymatcher","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"pathwaymatcher","identifiers":["doi:10.1093/GIGASCIENCE/GIZ088"],"license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"Pathwaymatcher is a software tool writen in java to search for pathways related to a list of proteins in reactome.","home_url":"https://github.com/PathwayAnalysisPlatform/PathwayMatcher","keywords":["Computational Biology","Gene Regulatory Networks","Humans","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide","Protein Interaction Mapping","Protein Processing, Post-Translational","Signal Transduction","Peptides"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"PathwayMatcher","home":"http://github.com/PathwayAnalysisPlatform/PathwayMatcher","summary":"Proteoform-centric network construction enables fine-granularity multiomics pathway mapping | PathwayMatcher is a free, open-source software to search for pathways related to a list of genes, proteins or proteoforms in Reactome | PathwayMatcher was benchmarked against different reference datasets covering multiple types of omics data | We present next the Cypher language queries to find the numbers shown in the summary statistics. These can also be used to get the protein-pathway mapping used in PathwayMatcher | PathwayMatcher is a standalone command line tool to match human biomedical data to pathways | PathwayMatcher is a standalone command line tool to match human biomedical data to pathways | 7448 valid tools on Nov 10, 2019","addition_date":"2019-11-14T18:02:37Z","last_update_date":"2021-01-05T09:45:47Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:PathwayMatcher","credit":[{"email":"marc.vaudel@uib.no","name":"Marc Vaudel","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1179-9578","typeEntity":"Person"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://github.com/PathwayAnalysisPlatform/PathwayMatcher/wiki"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://github.com/PathwayAnalysisPlatform/PathwayMatcher/wiki/Performance"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://github.com/PathwayAnalysisPlatform/PathwayMatcher/wiki/queries"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Expression profile pathway mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0533"},{"term":"Pathway or network comparison","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0277"},{"term":"Post-translation modification site prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0417"}]}],"name":"PathwayMatcher","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/GIGASCIENCE/GIZ088","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019 The Author(s) 2019. Published by Oxford University Press.Background: Mapping biomedical data to functional knowledge is an essential task in bioinformatics and can be achieved by querying identifiers (e.g., gene sets) in pathway knowledge bases. However, the isoform and posttranslational modification states of proteins are lost when converting input and pathways into gene-centric lists. Findings: Based on the Reactome knowledge base, we built a network of protein-protein interactions accounting for the documented isoform and modification statuses of proteins. We then implemented a command line application called PathwayMatcher (github.com/PathwayAnalysisPlatform/PathwayMatcher) to query this network. PathwayMatcher supports multiple types of omics data as input and outputs the possibly affected biochemical reactions, subnetworks, and pathways. Conclusions: PathwayMatcher enables refining the network representation of pathways by including proteoforms defined as protein isoforms with posttranslational modifications. The specificity of pathway analyses is hence adapted to different levels of granularity, and it becomes possible to distinguish interactions between different forms of the same protein.","authors":[{"name":"Barsnes H."},{"name":"Burger B."},{"name":"Fabregat A."},{"name":"Hermjakob H."},{"name":"Horro C."},{"name":"Johansson S."},{"name":"Njolstad P.R."},{"name":"Sanchez L.F.H."},{"name":"Vaudel M."}],"date":"2019-08-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"GigaScience","title":"PathwayMatcher: Proteoform-centric network construction enables fine-granularity multiomics pathway mapping"},"pmcid":"PMC6667378","pmid":"31363752"}],"topic":[{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"},{"term":"Protein modifications","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0601"},{"term":"Proteomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0121"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"PathwayMatcher","home":"https://bio.tools/PathwayMatcher","summary":"Proteoform-centric network construction enables fine-granularity multiomics pathway mapping | PathwayMatcher is a free, open-source software to search for pathways related to a list of genes, proteins or proteoforms in Reactome | PathwayMatcher was benchmarked against different reference datasets covering multiple types of omics data | We present next the Cypher language queries to find the numbers shown in the summary statistics. These can also be used to get the protein-pathway mapping used in PathwayMatcher | PathwayMatcher is a standalone command line tool to match human biomedical data to pathways | PathwayMatcher is a standalone command line tool to match human biomedical data to pathways | 7448 valid tools on Nov 10, 2019","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:pathwaymatcher/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":false,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":2,"citations":[{"count"